{"id":"sat-linear-equations","title":"SAT Math: linear equations and systems","subject":"Mathematics","label":"SAT","exams":["sat"],"language":"en","seconds":175,"duration":175.03,"audio":"voice.mp3","words":478,"sections":[{"id":"hook","title":"Phone plans","start":0,"end":18.315},{"id":"explain","title":"One variable","start":18.315,"end":52.155},{"id":"explain2","title":"Systems","start":52.155,"end":80.555},{"id":"example","title":"Worked example","start":80.555,"end":108.225},{"id":"check","title":"Quick check","start":108.225,"end":118.305},{"id":"answer","title":"Answer","start":118.305,"end":126.645},{"id":"mistakes","title":"Common mistakes","start":126.645,"end":149.525},{"id":"recap","title":"Recap","start":149.525,"end":175.03}],"lines":[{"s":0,"a":0.5,"b":8.15,"text":"Hi, I'm Kora. Imagine two phone plans. One charges a sign-up fee plus a monthly rate, and the other has no fee but a higher rate.","w":[0.5,0.74,0.97,1.32,1.79,2.03,2.38,2.8,3.03,3.5,3.62,4.09,4.33,4.62,4.74,5.21,5.56,5.8,6.03,6.38,6.62,6.8,7.03,7.27,7.38,7.8]},{"s":0,"a":8.45,"b":14.12,"text":"Which is cheaper, and when? That is linear equations and systems, and the SAT loves them.","w":[8.48,8.68,8.82,9.6,9.76,10.42,10.62,10.8,11.16,11.7,11.84,12.62,12.72,13,13.56,13.82]},{"s":0,"a":14.42,"b":17.89,"text":"By the end of this lesson, you will pick the right plan in seconds.","w":[14.5,14.66,14.84,14.98,15.08,15.26,15.92,16.04,16.22,16.42,16.58,16.8,17.22,17.36]},{"s":1,"a":18.74,"b":23.23,"text":"A linear equation has variables to the first power, and its graph is a straight line.","w":[18.82,18.9,19.3,19.74,19.92,20.4,20.52,20.66,20.96,21.72,21.82,21.98,22.36,22.48,22.58,22.94]},{"s":1,"a":23.53,"b":27.47,"text":"To solve one with a single variable, do the same thing to both sides.","w":[23.56,23.72,24.1,24.24,24.4,24.5,24.84,25.66,25.84,26.02,26.34,26.6,26.74,27]},{"s":1,"a":27.77,"b":33.5,"text":"Subtract the same number, add the same number, or divide both sides by the same nonzero number.","w":[27.88,28.4,28.56,28.84,29.58,29.76,29.88,30.12,30.74,30.9,31.32,31.6,31.96,32.12,32.26,32.6,33.16]},{"s":1,"a":33.8,"b":35.62,"text":"Keep it balanced, like a scale.","w":[33.82,34.06,34.2,34.84,35.06,35.16]},{"s":1,"a":35.92,"b":39.07,"text":"Slope intercept form is y equals m x plus b.","w":[36.02,36.36,36.86,37.12,37.44,37.62,38.12,38.36,38.52,38.82]},{"s":1,"a":39.37,"b":45.35,"text":"Here m is the slope, the rate of change, and b is the y intercept, the starting value.","w":[39.44,39.9,40,40.12,40.28,41.18,41.34,41.58,41.74,42.58,42.78,43.06,43.18,43.44,43.58,44.4,44.54,44.92]},{"s":1,"a":45.65,"b":49,"text":"SAT word problems often hide this as a fee plus a rate.","w":[45.84,46.26,46.5,47.08,47.36,47.62,47.9,48.04,48.16,48.44,48.72,48.8]},{"s":1,"a":49.3,"b":51.73,"text":"The fee is b, and the rate is m.","w":[49.34,49.52,49.82,49.96,50.56,50.66,50.82,51.26,51.56]},{"s":2,"a":52.58,"b":55.17,"text":"A system means two linear equations together.","w":[52.64,52.76,53.14,53.48,53.78,54.18,54.72]},{"s":2,"a":55.47,"b":58.45,"text":"Its solution is the point where the two lines cross.","w":[55.52,55.68,56.16,56.28,56.4,56.88,57.08,57.22,57.5,57.9]},{"s":2,"a":58.75,"b":60.8,"text":"That picture helps you predict the answer.","w":[58.78,59.04,59.42,59.66,59.82,60.26,60.44]},{"s":2,"a":61.1,"b":66.46,"text":"You can solve by substitution. Solve one equation for a variable, then plug that into the other.","w":[61.12,61.26,61.48,61.84,62.06,63.2,63.64,63.78,64.24,64.4,64.46,65.16,65.4,65.68,65.92,66.12,66.26]},{"s":2,"a":66.76,"b":71.16,"text":"Or use elimination. Add or subtract the equations to cancel one variable.","w":[66.8,67.04,67.24,68.54,68.74,68.86,69.3,69.42,69.96,70.08,70.52,70.68]},{"s":2,"a":71.46,"b":77.13,"text":"Parallel lines have the same slope but different intercepts, so they never cross and have no solution.","w":[71.46,72,72.38,72.54,72.68,73.02,73.6,73.76,74.14,74.98,75.12,75.36,75.66,76.16,76.3,76.5,76.7]},{"s":2,"a":77.43,"b":80.13,"text":"The same line has infinitely many solutions.","w":[77.44,77.68,78.04,78.38,78.68,79.22,79.48]},{"s":3,"a":80.98,"b":85.51,"text":"Let's solve x plus y equals ten and two x minus y equals five by elimination.","w":[81.02,81.24,81.76,81.94,82.34,82.5,82.82,83.08,83.22,83.52,83.68,84.12,84.24,84.52,84.82,84.96]},{"s":3,"a":85.81,"b":90.4,"text":"Add the equations. The y terms cancel, giving three x equals fifteen.","w":[85.88,86.06,86.22,87.08,87.38,87.52,87.84,88.54,88.9,89.34,89.56,89.86]},{"s":3,"a":90.7,"b":92.29,"text":"So x equals five.","w":[90.8,91.2,91.54,91.9]},{"s":3,"a":92.59,"b":98.64,"text":"Plug into x plus y equals ten. Five plus y equals ten, so y equals five.","w":[92.64,92.92,93.32,93.5,93.98,94.2,94.52,95.36,95.68,96.08,96.26,96.56,97.36,97.76,97.96,98.3]},{"s":3,"a":98.94,"b":103.72,"text":"Check both equations. Five plus five is ten, and two times five minus five is five.","w":[98.98,99.26,99.52,100.26,100.62,100.9,101.24,101.36,101.76,101.9,102.1,102.4,102.7,103,103.32,103.44]},{"s":3,"a":104.02,"b":107.8,"text":"Both work, so the solution is x equals five, y equals five.","w":[104.06,104.36,104.98,105.12,105.24,105.72,106.04,106.26,106.58,107.1,107.24,107.5]},{"s":4,"a":108.65,"b":112.32,"text":"Quick check. Solve three x plus seven equals twenty-two.","w":[108.65,109.04,109.49,109.87,110.26,110.39,110.71,111.1,111.55]},{"s":4,"a":112.62,"b":115.54,"text":"Subtract seven from both sides first, then divide.","w":[112.68,113.22,113.54,113.74,114.02,114.34,114.9,115.14]},{"s":4,"a":115.84,"b":117.88,"text":"Pause here and try it. I'll wait.","w":[115.88,116.22,116.52,116.64,116.92,117.34,117.54]},{"s":5,"a":118.73,"b":126.22,"text":"The answer is x equals five, because subtracting seven gives three x equals fifteen, then dividing by three gives five.","w":[118.76,118.94,119.3,119.7,119.92,120.28,120.96,121.24,121.86,122.22,122.52,122.92,123.12,123.44,124.38,124.56,125,125.18,125.52,125.86]},{"s":6,"a":127.07,"b":128.82,"text":"Watch three common mistakes.","w":[127.16,127.56,127.88,128.22]},{"s":6,"a":129.12,"b":134.77,"text":"First, sign errors when subtracting an equation. Change every sign in the equation you subtract.","w":[129.14,129.62,129.96,130.32,130.52,131.06,131.14,132.22,132.7,133,133.34,133.42,133.56,133.98,134.14]},{"s":6,"a":135.07,"b":138.88,"text":"Second, forgetting to distribute a negative across parentheses.","w":[135.18,135.96,136.42,136.54,137.14,137.24,137.72,138.16]},{"s":6,"a":139.18,"b":143.79,"text":"Third, answering x when the question asks for y or for x plus y.","w":[139.26,140.18,140.76,140.94,141.1,141.22,141.78,142.08,142.48,142.7,142.82,143.08,143.24,143.68]},{"s":6,"a":144.09,"b":149.1,"text":"On the SAT, read the last line again before you answer, and plug your answer back in.","w":[144.16,144.26,144.56,145.32,145.56,145.68,146.02,146.26,146.6,146.92,147.14,147.7,147.86,148.12,148.32,148.6,148.88]},{"s":7,"a":149.95,"b":152.51,"text":"Recap. Do the same thing to both sides.","w":[150,150.94,151.1,151.24,151.5,151.7,151.82,152.08]},{"s":7,"a":152.81,"b":157.77,"text":"In y equals m x plus b, m is slope and b is the starting value.","w":[152.9,153.38,153.62,154.16,154.44,154.64,154.92,155.72,155.82,155.98,156.5,156.66,156.92,157.04,157.14,157.44]},{"s":7,"a":158.07,"b":164.39,"text":"Systems solve where lines cross. Parallel means no solution, same line means infinitely many.","w":[158.16,158.64,159,159.22,159.62,160.56,161.1,161.42,161.62,162.62,162.92,163.22,163.58,164.08]},{"s":7,"a":164.69,"b":170.15,"text":"Exam tip: reread the final question and substitute your answer back into the original equation.","w":[164.8,165.22,165.94,166.38,166.54,166.86,167.44,167.62,168.14,168.38,168.68,168.94,169.14,169.26,169.7]},{"s":7,"a":170.45,"b":174.43,"text":"Thanks for learning with Knowzone. Keep practicing, and you will get faster.","w":[170.48,170.76,170.92,171.22,171.38,172.36,172.6,173.36,173.48,173.62,173.78,173.98]}],"scenes":[{"at":0.25,"heading":"Phone plans","items":[{"at":0.4,"kind":"text","text":"Two phone plans: flat fee + rate"},{"at":8.35,"kind":"text","text":"Which is cheaper, and when?"},{"at":14.32,"kind":"text","text":"Pick the right plan in seconds"}]},{"at":18.49,"heading":"One variable","items":[{"at":18.64,"kind":"term","text":"Linear equation","detail":"Variables to first power; graph is a straight line"},{"at":23.43,"kind":"text","text":"Do the same to both sides"},{"at":27.67,"kind":"text","text":"Add/subtract same number; divide by nonzero"}]},{"at":35.67,"heading":"Slope-intercept form","items":[{"at":35.82,"kind":"formula","text":"y = mx + b"},{"at":39.27,"kind":"term","text":"m","detail":"slope = rate of change"},{"at":39.27,"kind":"term","text":"b","detail":"y-intercept = starting value"},{"at":45.55,"kind":"text","text":"Word problems: fee + rate"},{"at":49.2,"kind":"text","text":"Fee = b; rate = m"}]},{"at":52.33,"heading":"Systems","items":[{"at":52.48,"kind":"term","text":"System","detail":"Two linear equations together"},{"at":55.37,"kind":"text","text":"Solution = point where lines cross"},{"at":61,"kind":"text","text":"Substitution: solve one, plug into other"},{"at":66.66,"kind":"text","text":"Elimination: add/subtract to cancel a variable"}]},{"at":71.21,"heading":"Number of solutions","items":[{"at":71.36,"kind":"text","text":"Parallel: same slope, different intercepts → no solution"},{"at":77.33,"kind":"text","text":"Same line → infinitely many solutions"}]},{"at":80.73,"heading":"Elimination example","items":[{"at":80.88,"kind":"formula","text":"x + y = 10; 2x − y = 5"},{"at":85.71,"kind":"formula","text":"(x+y)+(2x−y)=10+5"},{"at":85.71,"kind":"formula","text":"3x = 15"},{"at":90.6,"kind":"formula","text":"x = 5"}]},{"at":92.34,"heading":"Finish and check","items":[{"at":92.49,"kind":"formula","text":"5 + y = 10 → y = 5"},{"at":98.84,"kind":"formula","text":"5+5=10; 2(5)−5=5"},{"at":103.92,"kind":"formula","text":"(x, y) = (5, 5)"}]},{"at":108.22,"heading":"Quick check","items":[{"at":108.22,"kind":"question","text":"Solve 3x + 7 = 22."}]},{"at":118.48,"heading":"Answer","items":[{"at":118.63,"kind":"text","text":"Subtract 7, then divide by 3"},{"at":118.63,"kind":"formula","text":"3x + 7 = 22 → 3x = 15"},{"at":118.63,"kind":"formula","text":"3x = 15 → x = 5"}]},{"at":126.82,"heading":"Common mistakes","items":[{"at":126.97,"kind":"text","text":"Watch three common mistakes"},{"at":129.02,"kind":"wrong","text":"Sign errors when subtracting"},{"at":134.97,"kind":"wrong","text":"Forget to distribute negative"},{"at":139.08,"kind":"wrong","text":"Answer x when asked y or x+y"},{"at":143.99,"kind":"tip","text":"Reread the last line; plug your answer back in"}]},{"at":149.7,"heading":"Recap","items":[{"at":149.85,"kind":"text","text":"Do the same thing to both sides"},{"at":152.71,"kind":"formula","text":"y = mx + b"},{"at":152.71,"kind":"text","text":"m = slope; b = starting value"},{"at":157.97,"kind":"text","text":"Cross = solution; parallel = none; same line = infinite"},{"at":164.59,"kind":"tip","text":"Reread final question; substitute answer back"}]}],"check":{"at":118.13,"seconds":10,"question":"Solve 3x + 7 = 22.","answer":"x = 5; subtract 7: 3x = 15; divide by 3: x = 5."},"fps":30,"mouth":"","level":"","credits":[],"voice":"qwen3-tts-12hz-1.7b (cloned voice)"}